
  <main id="main">

    <section class="page-head">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow">Pricing &amp; how I work</span>
        <h1>Low entry cost. No hourly rates.</h1>
        <p class="lead">A "from" price to start, then a fixed quote for your scope before I build. You see an estimate before you pay.</p>
        <div class="btn-row">
          <a href="start" class="btn btn--primary">Get an estimate</a>
          <a href="#care" class="btn btn--ghost">Hosting &amp; Care</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- PRICE LIST -->
    <section class="section section--tint" id="builds" aria-labelledby="pricesTitle">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="price-head reveal">
          <div>
            <h2 id="pricesTitle">Public pricing</h2>
            <p class="muted">Prices in ZAR. "From" prices vary with complexity; third-party costs like domains and AI usage are quoted separately.</p>
          </div>
          <p class="callout"><strong>Nothing to pay until you accept a fixed quote.</strong> Then a 40% deposit gets the build going and comes off your project price; the balance is due on completion. Or pay monthly instead: <strong>R795 a month</strong>, nothing upfront except the first month.</p>
          <p class="callout callout--promise"><strong>My promise:</strong> a reply within an hour (7am to 9pm, every day), and your website live within 7 days of approving the design, or your first month of Care is free. <a class="inline-link" href="terms#promises">The details</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="price-cols reveal">
          <div class="price-group">
            <h3>AI &amp; automation</h3>
            <ul class="price-list price-list--compact">
              <li><a href="services#ai">AI assistant<small>Answers from your real prices, hours and services</small></a><span class="price"><small>from</small>R11,500</span></li>
              <li><a href="services#ai">AI assistant, full<small>WhatsApp, bookings, answers from your documents</small></a><span class="price"><small>from</small>R22,500</span></li>
              <li><a href="services#automation">Automation<small>Replace a repetitive manual task</small></a><span class="price"><small>from</small>R14,500</span></li>
              <li><a href="services#dashboards">Dashboard<small>Built on your real business data</small></a><span class="price"><small>from</small>R14,500</span></li>
              <li><a href="services#software">Custom software<small>Larger apps and integrations</small></a><span class="price"><small>from</small>R35,000</span></li>
            </ul>
            <p class="tiny muted" style="margin:0.6rem 0 0">Plus what the AI provider charges to run it, billed at cost — never marked up, never hidden in the price.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="price-group">
            <h3>Websites</h3>
            <ul class="price-list price-list--compact">
              <li><a href="services#websites">Quick website<small>1 page, live in about a day</small></a><span class="price"><small>from</small>R4,500</span></li>
              <li><a href="services#websites">Business website<small>Up to 4–5 pages, custom layout</small></a><span class="price"><small>from</small>R9,500</span></li>
              <li><a href="services#websites">Custom website<small>Booking, online shop, portals</small></a><span class="price"><small>from</small>R20,000</span></li>
              <li><a href="services#websites">Changes to a site<small>Text, hours, images, small content</small></a><span class="price"><small>from</small>R450</span></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="small muted price-foot">Larger projects (typically R35,000, R65,000 or R120,000 and up) use a 30–50% deposit split across milestones and are quoted individually. <a class="inline-link" href="terms">Deposit terms</a>.</p>
        <div class="gbp-band reveal">
          <span class="card__icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 21s-7-6.2-7-11.5A7 7 0 0 1 19 9.5C19 14.8 12 21 12 21z"/><circle cx="12" cy="9.5" r="2.5"/></svg></span>
          <div class="gbp-band__text"><h3>Not ready for a website? Start with Google.</h3><p>I set up (or fix) your Google profile: category, hours, prices, photos, first posts and a review QR card. <strong>R1,200, once-off</strong>, and it comes off your website if you build one within 90 days.</p></div>
          <div class="gbp-band__cta"><button type="button" class="btn btn--primary" data-gbp-open>Set up my Google profile</button><a class="inline-link small" href="services#google">What's included</a></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- FIRST YEAR EXAMPLE -->
    <section class="section section--tint" aria-labelledby="fyTitle">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section__head section__head--center reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">A worked example</span>
          <h2 id="fyTitle">What a first year actually looks like.</h2>
          <p>For an AI assistant with the first year of AI Care.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="table-wrap reveal" style="max-width:640px;margin-inline:auto">
          <table class="spec">
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>AI assistant</td><td class="price" style="text-align:right">R11,500</td></tr>
              <tr><td>AI Care, first year</td><td class="price" style="text-align:right">R8,500</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>Total, first year</strong></td><td class="price" style="text-align:right"><strong>R20,000</strong></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Deposit, when you accept the quote (40%)</td><td class="price" style="text-align:right">R8,000</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Balance on completion</td><td class="price" style="text-align:right">R12,000</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <div class="pm-band reveal">
          <h3>Rather not pay upfront? Pay monthly.</h3>
          <p>A one-page website and Care plan instead, for <strong>R795 a month for 12 months</strong>, with nothing to pay upfront except the first month. After 12 months it drops to <strong>R450 a month</strong> for Care. Spreading it out costs a little more (R9,540 over the first year, against R9,000 upfront), so pick whichever suits your cash flow. Ask for it with your quote: I’ll show both options.</p>
        </div>
        <p class="center small muted section__foot reveal">Domain registration is charged separately where applicable. Care is R450 a month or R4,500 a year after the first year, AI Care R850 a month or R8,500 a year (Hosting from R180 a month); development is one-off.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- HOSTING & CARE -->
    <section class="section" id="care" aria-labelledby="careTitle">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section__head section__head--center reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">Hosting &amp; Care</span>
          <h2 id="careTitle">Kept online and looked after, from R180 a month.</h2>
          <p>A website is only online while it's hosted, so hosting is a running cost, not optional — separate from the one-off build. Ongoing sites take a plan (below), paid monthly or yearly; event or once-off sites are hosted just for the period you need. You own your domain and can host elsewhere if you prefer.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid plans">
          <div class="card plan reveal">
            <h3>Hosting</h3>
            <div class="plan__price">R180<small>/month</small></div>
            <p class="plan__yearly">or <strong>R1,800 a year</strong> (2 months free)</p>
            <p>Online, secure and backed up.</p>
            <ul><li>Website hosting</li><li>SSL certificate (the padlock)</li><li>Domain management</li><li>Backups</li><li>Uptime monitoring, every 10 minutes</li><li>Hosting-related support</li></ul>
            <p class="small muted" style="margin-top:0.6rem">Does not include changes to the site.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card plan reveal">
            <h3>Care</h3>
            <div class="plan__price">R450<small>/month</small></div>
            <p class="plan__yearly">or <strong>R4,500 a year</strong> (2 months free)</p>
            <p>Everything in Hosting, and I look after it for you.</p>
            <ul><li>Everything in Hosting</li><li>Small changes done for you: prices, photos, hours, contact details (about an hour a quarter)</li><li>Your Google Business Profile kept up to date</li><li>A link your customers tap to leave you a Google review</li><li>A short monthly report: was your site up, and how fast it was</li></ul>
          </div>
          <div class="card plan plan--featured reveal">
            <span class="plan__flag">Recommended</span>
            <h3>AI Care</h3>
            <div class="plan__price">R850<small>/month</small></div>
            <p class="plan__yearly">or <strong>R8,500 a year</strong> (2 months free)</p>
            <p>For anything with AI in it. What it knows has to stay true, or it stops being useful.</p>
            <ul><li>Everything in Care</li><li>What your assistant knows kept current: prices, hours, services, staff</li><li>Its answers checked, and corrected when it gets something wrong</li><li>A monthly report of what it actually handled, and how much came in after hours</li><li>Priority support: same-day replies on weekdays</li></ul>
          </div>
          <div class="card plan reveal">
            <h3>Partner retainer</h3>
            <div class="plan__price">R6,500<small>/month</small></div>
            <p class="plan__yearly">or <strong>R65,000 a year</strong> (2 months free)</p>
            <p>The closest thing to having me on staff, at a fraction of a salary.</p>
            <ul><li>Everything in AI Care</li><li><strong>10 hours of development every month</strong>, used on whatever needs it</li><li>Unused hours roll over one month</li><li>You go to the front of the queue, always</li><li>No separate quote for anything that fits in the hours</li></ul>
            <p class="small muted" style="margin-top:0.6rem">For businesses that keep finding the next thing to build.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="offer-note" data-offer-note hidden></div>
        <ul class="plan-notes reveal">
          <li><strong>Pay monthly or yearly.</strong> Monthly: I email you a card payment link each month, or set up a bank stop order. Yearly: one payment and you get 2 months free.</li>
          <li><strong>New website?</strong> Your quote includes the first year of Care (R4,500), so you start fully looked after. After that, choose monthly or yearly, or switch to Hosting.</li>
          <li><strong>R500 off, every year:</strong> keep a small "Website by Re-Charge" link in your site's footer and your plan is R500 a year cheaper (R50 a month).</li>
          <li><strong>Refer a business:</strong> when a business you send me goes live, your next year of Care is free.</li>
          <li><strong>Already with me?</strong> You keep your current price until you choose to change plans.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- HOW WE WORK -->
    <section class="section section--tint" id="how-we-work" aria-labelledby="rulesTitle">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section__head reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">How I work</span>
          <h2 id="rulesTitle">The rules that keep projects fast and fair.</h2>
          <p>These apply to every project. They protect your budget as much as my time — and they're why I can keep prices this low.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rules reveal">
          <div class="rule"><h3>Fixed scope</h3><p>Every project has a defined scope before work starts, so both sides know what "done" means.</p></div>
          <div class="rule"><h3>Fixed price</h3><p>You get a fixed price for that scope. If the scope holds, the price holds.</p></div>
          <div class="rule"><h3>Quote, then deposit</h3><p>You accept a fixed quote online and pay the deposit before development begins — never before you've seen the price.</p></div>
          <div class="rule"><h3>You own it</h3><p>Your code, designs, data and domain are yours — move them if you ever leave.</p></div>
        </div>
        <p class="small muted section__foot reveal">Full terms — including refunds, revisions, delays, ownership and hosting — are on the <a class="inline-link" href="terms">Terms &amp; Deposit</a> page.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- FAQ -->
    <section class="section" id="faq" aria-labelledby="pricingFaqTitle">
      <div class="container container--narrow">
        <div class="section__head section__head--center reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">Pricing questions</span>
          <h2 id="pricingFaqTitle">Common questions about cost.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="faq reveal">
          <details class="faq__item"><summary>Why "from" prices instead of a fixed list?</summary><p>Because a one-page site and a booking site with payments are both "websites", but they aren't the same work. Starting prices tell you roughly where a project lands; the estimate in the Project Builder gets closer, and the final quote is exact.</p></details>
          <details class="faq__item"><summary>Is the estimate the final price?</summary><p>No. The estimate is indicative. I review your project, confirm the scope, and send a fixed quote before any development.</p></details>
          <details class="faq__item"><summary>When do I pay the deposit?</summary><p>Only after you've seen and accepted your fixed quote. I send the quote online; if you're happy, you accept it and pay the deposit by card (Yoco). It comes off your total, and the balance is due on completion. Asking for a quote is free.</p></details>
          <details class="faq__item"><summary>Can I pay monthly instead?</summary><p>Yes, for websites. A one-page site with Care is R795 a month for 12 months, with only the first month to pay upfront, then R450 a month for Care. It costs a little more than paying upfront (R9,540 over the year, against R9,000), and the minimum is 12 months. Your quote can show both, and you pick.</p></details>
          <details class="faq__item"><summary>What does a typical first project cost?</summary><p>Most first projects are an AI assistant (from R11,500) or a one-page site (from R4,500). They're quick to deliver and a low-risk way to see how I work before anything bigger. Minor changes to an existing site start from R250.</p></details>
          <details class="faq__item"><summary>Can I start small and add to it later?</summary><p>Yes — that's the idea. A one-page website is an entry point, not the end product. Many clients add a dashboard, automation or a custom tool later, each quoted as its own small project.</p></details>
          <details class="faq__item"><summary>Is hosting required?</summary><p>Some hosting is needed to keep a site online — but not necessarily mine. Ongoing sites take an annual plan; event or once-off sites only need short-term hosting. You can also host elsewhere or provide your own; you always own your domain.</p></details>
          <details class="faq__item"><summary>What about AI running costs?</summary><p>Third-party AI/API usage is billed separately, based on actual usage, and explained before I build. I never bundle unlimited AI usage into a fixed price.</p></details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="cta" aria-labelledby="pricingCtaTitle">
      <div class="container cta__inner reveal">
        <span class="cta__services">Estimate first · Fixed quote before I build</span>
        <h2 id="pricingCtaTitle">See what your project would cost.</h2>
        <p>Describe it in the Project Builder and get an indicative estimate straight away. I send a fixed quote — you pay the deposit only once you accept it.</p>
        <div class="btn-row btn-row--center">
          <a href="start" class="btn btn--light btn--large">Start a Project</a>
          <button type="button" class="btn btn--free btn--large" data-mockup-open>Get a mockup <span class="btn__tag">Free</span></button>
        </div>
        <p class="small muted" style="margin-top:0.2rem">Not ready to commit? The mockup costs nothing — no deposit, no obligation.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>

